 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Thousands marched on the climate summit. With five days left, can it deliver?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Police put Saturday's crowd in Antalya, Turkey, at more than seven thousand, AFP reports. Environmental groups, trade unions and rights organisations led the march, which ended without major incident. Protesters said the summit is failing the communities hit hardest."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "One activist told AFP that host Turkey still has no roadmap to phase out fossil fuels, while new power stations and coal mines open. Inside, U.N. climate chief Simon Stiell urged countries to tackle the hardest issues and avoid tactical delays."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Formal talks pause on Sunday. From Monday, negotiators have five days to agree the wording of a final deal. Chris Bowen, who leads the negotiations, expects a first draft next week. The United States is skipping the talks for a second year."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will COP thirty-one reach a deal on time? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
